{
  "name": "cay_bang",
  "kind": "plant",
  "sources": [
    "A cây bàng (Terminalia catappa, the sea almond), a common tree of the streets and the beaches of Việt Nam (World Agroforestry, the species page; Thomson and Evans, Terminalia catappa, Species Profiles for Pacific Island Agroforestry, 2006).",
    "The species: 15 to 25 m high, a crown as wide as the tree is high, branches almost level in tiers of 4 or 5, 1 to 2 m apart (the pagoda form), leaves of 15 to 36 cm that are dark green and shine, and red or yellow before they fall, a bark that is gray-brown with cracks.",
    "Here: a street tree, 9 m high and 9 m wide, with a trunk of 0.5 m at its foot and four tiers (the sizes of a street tree are a guess from photos).",
    "It is from edits only: no code of World knows this kind of model."
  ],
